+    rustc_attr!(rustc_cxx_wrapper, "opts an inherent method on a `#[repr(cpp)]` type out of P09.3's auto-export (used by wrapper methods that call through to `extern \"C++\"` decls)"),
+    // P09.23: `#[rustc_cxx_drop_wrapper]` — trait-impl analogue of
+    // `#[rustc_cxx_wrapper]`. Applied to the `drop` method in an
+    // `impl Drop for T` where `T` is `#[repr(cpp)]`, it opts that
+    // method out of P09.15's auto-emission of the Itanium D0/D1/D2
+    // destructor variants. Used by `cxx_class_native!` when the
+    // C++ side already defines the destructor, so the Rust Drop
+    // body is just a thin forwarder to an `extern "C++"` decl.
+    rustc_attr!(rustc_cxx_drop_wrapper, "opts a `Drop::drop` impl on a `#[repr(cpp)]` type out of P09.15's D0/D1/D2 auto-emission (used when the C++ side already defines the destructor)"),
+    // P09.24: marks an inherent method on a `#[repr(cpp)]` type as
+    // a virtual member function. The compiler collects all methods
